  {
   "id": 61,
   "type": "MarkdownNote",
   "pos": [
    1500,
    40
   ],
   "size": [
    900,
    1000
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 0,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "title": "How this works",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "**Qwen 3D character: re-pose and re-camera her, then let Qwen redraw it**\n\nRuns on top of the same pieces as *Qwen Mannequin Edit* (Sapiens2 + SAM 3D Body fit), but instead of editing the photo in place it builds her as a posable 3D body and renders a new view.\n\n**How to use**\n1. Load her picture in **1 · Source image** and run once. The fitted body keeps her proportions (bust, waist, hips) from the photo.\n2. **Camera**: set *yaw* (orbit) / *pitch* / *zoom* in *MHR View Render*. Colours are projected from the photo; surface the photo never saw comes out smeared and Qwen fills it in.\n3. **Pose**: un-bypass (Ctrl+B) the *Pose reference* loader and its *Pose of the reference image* node; the pose is copied onto her body.\n4. **Outfit / character references**: un-bypass the reference loaders you need, set *Image Pick* to **b** (grey mannequin), and name them in the prompt (`<image2>` = outfit, `<image3>` = other character).\n5. **Prompt only**: leave every loader bypassed, keep Image Pick on **a**, write what you want.\n\nEvery preview shows what goes into Qwen: the control depth (near = bright), the grey mannequin and the textured render.\n\n*First version: pose copy and camera orbit are geometry only; check the previews before spending a Qwen run on them.*"
   ],
   "widgets_values_named": {
    "text": "**Qwen mannequin edit, planned by a VLM**\n\n0. **Plan** - type the edit in plain words. A Qwen3-VL reads the image and instruction and decides: the edit type (outfit / recolour / local / background / pose), whether the body silhouette changes (only then is the mannequin control used), which parts of the old outfit are removed (-> negative prompt, and hair/glasses dropped from the silhouette), and it writes what must stay the same (face, hair, build, pose, camera, framing, background) into the prompt, even if you did not mention it.\n1. **Perception** - Sapiens2 splits the figure into skin (trusted) vs clothing/armor, and measures the clothed depth.\n2. **Mannequin** - SAM 3D Body base body, refit with bounded sliders to match visible skin and stay inside the clothed silhouette; real depth where skin is visible, fitted body where clothing hides it.\n3. **Edit** - the mannequin depth drives the Qwen Union control (strength 0.8, end 0.8 from the planner) so the body is fixed and the prompt changes the clothes. For recolours and small edits the planner switches the control off and stages 1-2 are skipped (lazy gates), so the edit is a plain reference edit.\n\n**Knobs**: planner `force_mannequin` (auto/on/off), `mannequin_strength`, `mannequin_end`, base negative. Check the previews: enriched prompt, plan, regions, mannequin, control depth."
   },
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  }
